cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "TEXAS: Temperature Estimation via a Bayesian Approach with Stan"
message: "If you use this software, please cite it using the metadata from this file."
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Rattanasriampaipong
    given-names: Ronnakrit
version: 0.1.0
date-released: "2026-03-10"
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/PaleoLipidRR/TEXAS"
# doi: 10.5281/zenodo.XXXXXXX  # add upon Zenodo upload
abstract: >
  TEXAS (texas-psm) is a Python package for Bayesian GDGT-temperature calibration
  using Stan. It implements a two-stage workflow: forward calibration of a
  generalized logistic curve (Ring Index to temperature) using hierarchical
  Bayesian Stan models, and inverse temperature reconstruction from new Ring Index
  observations with full posterior uncertainty.
keywords:
  - paleoceanography
  - paleothermometry
  - GDGT
  - TEX86
  - Bayesian statistics
  - Stan
  - Python
